All-in-One Blender Guide: Roblox Rigging, 3-Ending Maze Animation & GitHub Upload
PART 1: Fast, Lag-Free Viewport Setup
While Moving & Animating: Click the Solid Mode sphere (2nd circle at the top-right of the 3D Viewport). Because Texture color mode is set, you will still see all brick, tile, and wood textures with zero lag.
To Preview Orb Glare: Click Material Preview (3rd circle), click the small down-arrow v next to the shading circles, and set Compositor to Always (or Disabled while editing so it never lags).
Set Timeline Length: At the bottom-right of the Timeline, change End from 250 to 400.
PART 2: Rigging Your Roblox Character (Rigid Blocky Limbs)
Step 2.1 — Separate the 6 Body Blocks (If Imported as 1 Combined Mesh)
Click the Roblox character and press Tab (Edit Mode).
Press A (Select All), then press P → By Loose Parts.
Press Tab back to Object Mode so Head, Torso, Left Arm, Right Arm, Left Leg, and Right Leg are separate blocks.
Step 2.2 — Build the 6 Bones (Armature)
Press Numpad 1 (Front View) and press Shift + A → Armature → Single Bone.
Go to Object Data Properties (green running stick-figure icon on the right), open Viewport Display, and check [x] In Front.
Press Tab (Edit Mode on the Armature):
Torso Bone: Place the bottom ball at the waist and the top tip at the neck. Press F2 and name it Torso.
Head Bone: Click the top tip of Torso and press E → Z to extrude straight up into the head. Name it Head.
Arm.L & Arm.R Bones: Press Shift + A to add a bone. Place its thick ball (base) at the top shoulder joint and its pointy tip pointing down to the hand. Name it Arm.L, then duplicate (Shift + D → X) to the right arm and name it Arm.R.
Leg.L & Leg.R Bones: Duplicate a bone (Shift + D), place its thick ball (base) at the hip joint (top of the leg) and its pointy tip pointing down to the foot. Name it Leg.L, then duplicate (Shift + D → X) to the right leg and name it Leg.R.
Link Limb Bones to the Torso Bone:
Still in Edit Mode, hold Shift and select Arm.L, Arm.R, Leg.L, and Leg.R, then Shift-click Torso last.
Press Ctrl + P → Keep Offset.
Step 2.3 — Attach the Blocky Body Parts to the Bones (Bone Parenting)

(Do NOT use Automatic Weights, or the blocky arms and legs will bend like rubber!)

Press Tab back to Object Mode.
Click the Left Arm mesh, then Shift-click the Armature.
Switch to Pose Mode (Ctrl + Tab), click the Arm.L bone, and press Ctrl + P → Bone.
Press Ctrl + Tab back to Object Mode and repeat for:
Right Arm → Arm.R
Left Leg → Leg.L
Right Leg → Leg.R
Head → Head
Torso → Torso
Step 2.4 — Create an Automatic Running Loop (20 Frames)
Click the Armature and enter Pose Mode (Ctrl + Tab).
Frame 1: Rotate Leg.L and Arm.R forward (R → X → 35 → Enter). Rotate Leg.R and Arm.L backward (R → X → -35 → Enter). Press A (select all bones) and press I → Rotation.
Frame 10: Flip them (Leg.L & Arm.R to -35°, Leg.R & Arm.L to +35°). Press A and I → Rotation.
Frame 20: Copy the Frame 1 keyframes (Ctrl + C then Ctrl + V in the Timeline).
Press A in the Timeline and press Shift + E → Make Cyclic (F-Modifier). Now his arms and legs run automatically for all 400 frames while you move the Armature in Object Mode!
PART 3: Animating the 3 Maze Endings (Frames 1 – 400)

Switch to Object Mode, select your Character Armature, and press Numpad 7 (Top View) to see the maze corridors from above.

ENDING 1 (Frames 1 – 129): Finishes Without the Chest

Story: Enters at Start, gets blocked by debris, skips the chest, and exits empty-handed.

Frame 1 (Start Gate): Move the character to the front-left Start Gate (Z = 0). Press I → Location & Rotation.
Frame 20: Move him (G → Shift + Z) down the first corridor (I → Location & Rotation).
Frame 45 (Blocked by Debris): Move him right in front of Blocking_Corridor_Debris (I → Location & Rotation).
At Frame 50 and Frame 55, rotate him (R → Z) left and right so he looks at the rubble and backs off.
Frame 75: Move him along the detour corridor past the Treasure Chest room without going inside (I → Location & Rotation).
Frame 95: Move him around the back-right corridor (I → Location & Rotation).
Frame 120 (Exits Empty-Handed): Move him out the back-right Exit Gate (I → Location & Rotation).
Frame 129 (Hold Before Reset): In the Timeline, click the Frame 120 keyframe, press Shift + D, and drag the copy to Frame 129.
ENDING 2 (Frames 130 – 239): Cursed Jump (Trap_PowerUp_Orb) → Stuck in 4-Wall Box

Story: Resets to Start, grabs the pink Trap_PowerUp_Orb, jumps over 1 wall into the sealed 4-wall prison cell (4, 2), and gets trapped!

Frame 130 (Instant Teleport Back to Start):
Move the playhead to Frame 130 (1 frame after 129 so he teleports cleanly without sliding through walls!).
Move the character back to the Start Gate (Z = 0) and press I → Location & Rotation.
Frame 150: Move him up the left corridor (I → Location & Rotation).
Frame 170 (Touches Pink Trap_PowerUp_Orb):
Move him onto Trap_PowerUp_Orb (I → Location & Rotation).
Hide the Pink Orb on Pickup: Click Trap_PowerUp_Orb, press I → Scale at Frame 169, then at Frame 170 press S → 0 → Enter and I → Scale.
Frame 182 (Peak of Cursed Jump Over 1 Wall):
Select your character again. Move him halfway across the single wall behind the orb and lift him high in the air (G → Z → 2.7 → Enter) so he clears the 2.3m wall (I → Location & Rotation).
Frame 195 (Lands Inside Sealed 4-Wall Trap Cell):
Move him inside the sealed square room with Trapped_Box_Cell_Shards and bring him down to the floor (Z = 0, I → Location & Rotation).
Frames 205 – 239 (Stuck Inside the Walls):
Keyframe him bumping into the 4 sealed walls and turning around at Frames 205, 215, and 225.
Duplicate (Shift + D) the Frame 225 keyframe to Frame 239.
ENDING 3 (Frames 240 – 400): Invincibility Orb → Grabs Treasure_Chest → Overcomes All Traps!

Story: Resets to Start, vaults the barricade, grabs the Cyan Invincibility Orb, picks up the Treasure_Chest, and barges through the spikes, swinging axe, and falling debris out the Exit!

Frame 240 (Teleport Back to Start):
Move your character back to the Start Gate (Z = 0) at Frame 240 (I → Location & Rotation).
(Optional): Click Trap_PowerUp_Orb, press Alt + S at Frame 240 to restore its size, and press I → Scale.
Frames 265 – 275 (Jumps Over Wooden_Barricade_Obstacle_1):
Move him up to Wooden_Barricade_Obstacle_1 at Frame 265 (Z = 0), hop over it at Frame 270 (Z = 1.1m), and land on the other side at Frame 275 (Z = 0).
Frame 285 (Grabs Cyan Invincibility_PowerUp_Orb):
Move him onto Invincibility_PowerUp_Orb at Frame 285 (I → Location & Rotation).
Click Invincibility_PowerUp_Orb, press I → Scale at Frame 284, then at Frame 285 press S → 0 → Enter and I → Scale.
Frame 310 (Reaches & Picks Up Treasure_Chest Using Child Of):
Move your character right next to Treasure_Chest at Frame 310 (I → Location & Rotation).
Attach the Chest ONLY from Frame 310 onward:
Click Treasure_Chest → go to Object Constraints Properties (blue gear-with-chain icon on the right).
Click Add Object Constraint → Child Of and set Target to your Character Armature.
Click Set Inverse.
At Frame 309, set Influence = 0.000 and press I while hovering over Influence (keeps the chest on its pedestal during Endings 1 & 2!).
At Frame 310, set Influence = 1.000 and press I over Influence.
Frames 310 – 400 (Runs Invincible Through All Traps to the Exit):
Frame 335: Move character straight across Spike_Trap_Spikes_2 (I → Location & Rotation).
Frame 355: Move character straight through Swing_Trap_Pendulum_Blade (I → Location & Rotation).
Frame 375: Jump over Wooden_Barricade_Obstacle_2 (Z = 1.1m at 375, Z = 0 at 382).
Frame 400: Run out the Exit Gate carrying the Treasure_Chest (I → Location & Rotation)!
PART 4: Animating the Traps & Power-Up Orb Glow
Swinging Pendulum Axe (Swing_Trap_Pendulum_Blade):
Click Swing_Trap_Pendulum_Blade → open Object Properties (orange square icon).
Frame 1: Set Rotation Y = -40°, press I.
Frame 20: Set Rotation Y = 40°, press I.
Frame 40: Set Rotation Y = -40°, press I.
In the Timeline, press A then Shift + E → Make Cyclic (F-Modifier) so the axe swings continuously!
Floor Spikes Shooting Up (Spike_Trap_Spikes_2):
Click Spike_Trap_Spikes_2.
Frame 325: Location Z = -0.35 m (hidden inside floor), press I.
Frame 332: Location Z = 0.08 m (spikes shoot up right as he runs over them invincible!), press I.
Frame 350: Location Z = -0.35 m, press I.
Falling Escape Debris (Escape_Debris_Rock_1 to 5):
Select each rock: at Frame 315, move it up (G → Z → 2.6) and press I → Location.
At Frame 328, move it down to the floor (Z = 0.22) and press I → Location.
Pulsing Glare on the Power-Up Orbs (Optional):
Click Invincibility_PowerUp_Orb (or Trap_PowerUp_Orb), open the Shader Editor, and keyframe Emission → Strength (4.5 at Frame 1 → 9.0 at Frame 20 → 4.5 at Frame 40, then Shift + E → Make Cyclic).
